 ["THE MAP gives one checker on the machine all the time, to be reached from every place text is written, VS Code, the CLI, Smile Chat, the Pi harness, Notepad and Google Docs through the clipboard. Today it reaches VS Code, the CLI and the hook on every file written. It writes the footer when a header is finished and mends on save, and never changes a word of mine. Its conventions are four spaces per depth, a footer that mirrors its header's faces and reads End followed by its name, a trailing face never larger than the leading one, and no Markdown heading inside a section. A file is finished when the checker answers \"Every face meets the conventions.\""
